es 'You want to keep the investment strategy of your pension fairly simple' [P5], yet recommends a complex multi-asset solution with ongoing rebalancing and adviser management required","No documented discussion of the client's limited knowledge of stocks and shares, pensions or enterprise schemes appears in the file; the investor experience notes section shows 'No additional notes were recorded' [P10]"],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The requirement asks whether the client's knowledge, experience and investment understanding are accurately reflected, whether recommended product complexity is consistent with demonstrated knowledge and experience, and whether rationale is adequately justified.\n\nOn reflection of the facts: The canonical model records the client's stated level as 'Moderate' and the recommended products as 'Complex'. The questionnaire completed at [P9] is the primary evidence of the client's actual knowledge and experience. It records 'No understanding / knowledge' on three critical investment and pension topics. The client has no recent personal experience with stocks and shares, unit trusts, pensions or enterprise schemes—only with basic savings and cash accounts.\n\nThe report reproduces a description of a Balanced investor (Risk Rating 5) that begins with a conditional: 'If you have some experience in investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters then you may be suited to a Balanced approach' [P1, P6, P7, P19]. This conditional is restated in the suitability report at [P7]: 'If you have some experience in investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters, then you may be suited to a Balanced approach to investing.' The precondition is 'some experience in investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters'. The questionnaire evidence contradicts this precondition: the client reports no understanding of stocks and shares or pensions, and no recent experience with investment product