g ongoing rebalancing and adviser discretion) is not proportionate to the client's demonstrated knowledge level (no understanding of stocks and shares, pensions or investment schemes, experience limited to cash accounts). The rationale offered focuses on why the CIP structure is better than an investment pathway, not on why it is appropriate for a client with the client's limited knowledge.\n\nThe vulnerability overlay does not apply here; no vulnerabilities affecting knowledge or comprehension are recorded in the evidence.","citations":[{"passageId":"P9","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"Do you understand how stocks and shares work and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge. Do you understand how Enterprise Investment Schemes and Venture Capital Trusts work and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge. Do you understand how pension planning and income in retirement works and do you know the risks associated with them? No understanding / knowledge. Have you invested in Unit Trusts and General Investment Accounts within the last 5 years? No. Have you invested in stocks and shares within the last 5 years? No. Have you invested in pension planning and income in retirement products within the last 5 years? No.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"No additional notes were recorded","cells":null},{"passageId":"P7","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"If you have some experience in investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters, then you may be suited to a Balanced approach to investing.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"If you have some experience of investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters then you may be suited to a Balanced approach to investing.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P5","source":"Suitability Report