ment states 'You should retain the services of a financial adviser. You'll need an adviser if you want to make certain changes to your Pension Portfolio' but does not specify implementation responsibility for pension transfers or encashments. Scottish Widows Policy Info confirms the plan exists but provides no implementation timescale or process detail. The intelliflo planning scenarios are forward-looking analyses with no implementation instruction detail. The Risk profile report contains no implementation guidance.","discrepancies":["The report assigns 'Adviser' as responsible party for three Switch recommendations but does not state who is responsible for the Retain recommendation (EA4) or the Encash recommendation (Scottish Widows).","The report states a general timescale of '10-15 working days' but does not specify whether this applies equally to all three Switch actions or whether individual arrangements (People's Pension, Scottish Widows encashment, Aviva switch) have different timescales.","The nomination of beneficiaries form is stated to be 'provided to you after the transfer process is begun' but no action is attributed to adviser or client to initiate or complete this step beyond the recommendation that the client 'complete' it.","The Encash recommendation for Scottish Widows (£211.32 plan) has no stated implementation timescale or responsible party, unlike the Switch recommendations.","The Retain recommendation (EA4 - Zurich at £103,439.24) has no stated implementation timescale or responsible party."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The requirement asks whether recommendations state what action will be taken, when it will be taken, and by whom, where material to suitability. The report does state actions (Switch, Retain, Encash) and provides a general timescale (10-15 working days) and identifies the adviser as responsible for the three Switch recommendations. However, material gaps exist: (1) Two of five recommendations (Reta