heaper' is contradicted by its own projected values. The initial impact is also negative: switching creates an immediate £3,305 shortfall in fund value [P1, P10]. The reduction in yield at 2.1%-2.3% [P10] is substantially higher than the existing arrangement at 0.3%, meaning charges are eating into returns more aggressively in the new solution. The report states ongoing adviser charge of 1.00% [P3] which has been 'considered as part of the new solution projections' but the discrepancy between the stated 0.24% charge saving and the 4.24% required outperformance suggests the adviser fee impact is not clearly explained or reconciled with the charge comparison. The critical yields required (up to 7.8%) are significantly higher than historical growth rates typically available, indicating substantial headwinds from charges. The report fails to adequately disclose or explain why a 'cheaper' solution produces materially worse projected retirement values across all growth scenarios.","citations":[{"passageId":"P10","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Low growth rate (0.00%)","Existing pension","£108,000","New solution","£97,600","Effect of switching","£10,400 or 9.6% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Mid growth rate (2.95%)","Existing pension","£127,000","New solution","£115,000","Effect of switching","£12,000 or 9.4% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["High growth rate (5.88%)","Existing pension","£150,000","New solution","£135,000","Effect of switching","£15,000 or 10.0% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":"Reduction in yield: 2.1%, 2.2%, 2.3%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":"Existing pension: £110,185.60. New solution day one: £106,880.