hat should this high level of inflation continue at the assumed rate, there would be no shortfall that requires your pension or investment funds to be used.","cells":null},{"passageId":"[P3]","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Low growth rate - (0.00%)","Projected value at age 75","£108,000","£97,600","Effect of switching","-","£10,400 or 9.6% decrease"]},{"passageId":"[P2]","source":"Key Features (1).md","category":"H","quote":"The value of your pension pot and the retirement benefits it can provide may go down as well as up. You could get back less than has been invested.","cells":null},{"passageId":"[P7]","source":"Key Features (1).md","category":"H","quote":"If you withdraw high levels of income, there'll be less money to provide for dependants or to buy a lifetime annuity in the future, should you want to. Your investments need to grow to compensate for the income you withdraw. If that doesn't happen, the income you take will deplete your pension fund. Especially if you choose to take a high level of income.","cells":null},{"passageId":"[P10]","source":"Illustration - new.md","category":"H","quote":"Your pension fund could be worth £97,500 [Lower 1.9%], £115,000 [Medium 5%], £135,000 [Higher 8%]","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Disclosure shortfall","Weak justification"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

