esilience factors","Support needs adjustments or accommodations made to the advice process, communication method, or explanation","Evidence of any identified comprehension requirements, accessibility needs, or literacy considerations","Documentation of third-party involvement, Power of Attorney, trusted contact arrangements, or family support requests","Individualised notes or case-specific discussion records of capacity for loss or support needs beyond template text"],"analysis":"The requirement asks whether information in the suitability report relating to vulnerabilities, support needs, communication preferences, capacity, comprehension requirements, and duty of care considerations is fully supported by evidence. The comparison cannot be performed because the report makes no extraction-level assertions at the canonical model paths for adjustments made or characteristics recorded. The extraction metadata confirms these are NotPresentInDocument. This means one of two things: either the report contains no such information, or the extraction failed to capture it. Reviewing the passages: the report does reference capacity for loss [P5], Power of Attorney [P4], and communication preference [P2], but these are generic or standard statements. The capacity assessment text appears verbatim in both the report [P5] and file notes [P11], suggesting template language. The Risk profile report sections for 'Capacity for loss questionnaire' and 'Investor Experience' both state 'No additional notes were recorded' [P19, P23], indicating the vulnerability assessment process, if conducted, was not documented with client-specific findings. No vulnerability characteristics are identified anywhere in the file. No support needs adjustments are recorded. No comprehension accommodations are evidenced. The Power of Attorney recommendation [P4] is phrased as general prudence ('It would also be prudent...') rather than a response to identified risk. The communication preference 'No Preference' [P2] with email marketing consent shows a channel preference was recorded, but the suitability report does not reference it or tailor its language, format, or explanation to any identified accessibility or comprehension need. The file contains no evidence of a vulnerability overlay applied to the suitability assessment or recommendations. Per the requirement's decision logic, the absence of vulnerability assessment documentation in a case with income vulnerability indicators (household income insufficient to meet stated expenditure without pension assets, negative monthly disposable income of -£288 [P8]) and a client aged 69 approaching retirement constitutes a process risk. The FG21/1 drivers (life event of retirement, low resilience shown by expenditure exceeding income, capability in pension decisions limited to workplace schemes [P5]) were not flagged or addressed through individualised support measures documented in the file. The standard-form capacity assessment and generic Power of Attorney suggestion do not constitute tailored support to meet identified comprehension or support needs.","citations":[{"passageId":"P5","source":"Suitability Report","category":"I","quote":"John, you are aware that investment values can rise as well as fall, and although your experience is limited to your workplace pension arrangements, you understand that returns are not guaranteed. You confirmed that any potential underperformance would not have a detrimental impact on your day-to-day living.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Suitability Report","category":"I","quote":"It would also be prudent to set up and register Power of Attorney for your financial affairs / health and welfare, to ensure that in the event of your incapacity, your spouse or relative could act on your behalf.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P2","source":"Fact Find","category":"B","quote":"Preferred delivery method: No Preference","cells":null},{"passageId":"P19","source":"Risk profile report","category":"D","quote":"Capacity for loss questionnaire: No additional notes were recorded","cells":null},{"passageId":"P23","source":"Risk profile report","category":"D","quote":"Investor Experience: No additional notes were recorded","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Fact Find","category":"B","quote":null,"cells":["Total Monthly Household Expenditure","£1,718.00","Total Net Monthly Income","£1,430.00","Total Monthly Disposable Income","£-288.00"]},{"passageId":"P11","source":"File notes","category":"C","quote":"XXXX, you are aware that investment values can rise as well as fall, and although your experience is limited to your workplace pension arrangements, you understand that returns are not guaranteed. You confirmed that any potential underperformance would not have a detrimental impact on your day-to-day living.","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Missing evidence","Process risk"],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

